# L §2.4 Short form: "a def with one rule labelled base, no v, no when, no own governs, no notes prints as
# def x: T = expr at E" (u; w keeps its note, z its when, so both stay long). "Inside a section: notes come first,
# then rules (sorted by label, then by the known date of their v, a rule without v first, then by the start of their
# own governs)" (y: a before b; base without v before base with v; v2 known before v1). "A beats list is sorted by
# label, with ', '" (y's rule a, and the replace rule in the version).
=== options reprint
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

def u: num at 2026-12-31
  rule base = (1)
def w: num
  note "kept long"
  rule base = 1
def z: num
  rule base = 1 when c
def y: int
  rule b = 1
  rule base v v1 = 4
  rule base v v2 = 3
  rule base = 0
  rule a beats c,b = 2

version v1
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-05-01
  replace rule y.b beats zz, base = 7
version v2
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-02-01
